      "side": 1,
      "message": "So I think I have concluded on what to do here:\n\n2 tearDown paths:\n- internal, an error occured. This could also lead to a restart.\n- external, the request(s) went away.\n\n1) The respective offers should handle internal tear down, as the code is not shared between the two. This means, the L2capNetwork can\u0027t just post a common Message on the handler. It should receive a callback object that includes an onError() and onNetworkUnwanted() callback. It\u0027s possible that the two are handled the same, which remains to be seen.\n\n2) to clean up this file, L2capNetwork should be moved out. This code should only concern itself with bringing up and keeping track of those networks, not the networks themselves.\n\n3) Similarly, L2capPacketForwarder will take a onError callback object. That will just forward to L2capNetwork\u0027s onError callback.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 107,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 107,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "6f167694b45d58128fce331b104e364e16edb192",
