      "writtenOn": "2025-02-06T19:41:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The NetworkRequest shouldn\u0027t be passed here, or to the ConnectThread. Calling declareNetworkRequestUnfulfillable from within this context is broken as there might already be another request present (that will then never be fulfilled). The only context declareNetworkRequestUnfulfillable can be called from is directly from within onNetworkNeeded().\n\nI think this also means that declareNetworkRequestUnfulfillable() cannot be called when any of the Bluetooth APIs fail, because those will be called again on restart. Otherwise, we must track all requests for a given network and send onUnavailable to all of them.\n\nInstead, retrying with exponential backoff might be the better option.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 524,
        "startChar": 47,
        "endLine": 524,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "6f167694b45d58128fce331b104e364e16edb192",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
