      "writtenOn": "2025-02-06T19:41:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This code should be refactored into a handleCreateBluetoothSocket() function. If it fails, it cannot call declareNetworkRequestUnfulfillable, it must post delayed on the handler (that\u0027s not great because time doesn\u0027t count when the device is asleep, the timeout used here shouldn\u0027t be more than a few seconds (5 or 10 maybe)). It\u0027s probably best for the client to create the network request with a timeout, to figure out whether the network was actually created. The most likely failure path here is bluetooth being turned off, or the other device not being reachable.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 678,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 701,
        "endChar": 94
      },
      "revId": "6f167694b45d58128fce331b104e364e16edb192",
